menu "PlantHub Zigbee"

config PLANTHUB_ZB_ENABLED
    bool "Enable the Zigbee coordinator"
    default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32H2
    default n
    help
        The Zigbee coordinator, which since 2026-10 runs only on the ESP32-H2
        of the two-chip hub (planthubos/h2fw/, which pulls this component in and needs
        an 802.15.4 radio plus the zb_storage/zb_fct partitions). The C6 hub
        builds keep it off -- a C6 never runs a coordinator itself; its only
        use was the retired Zigbee bridge node -- and talk to the H2 over
        h2_link instead. The component still compiles on the C6 as stubs.

config PLANTHUB_ZB_PERMIT_JOIN_S
    int "Permit-join window (seconds)"
    default 180
    range 30 254
    help
        How long the network accepts new devices after the user presses
        Pair. The window is a window, never a mode: it closes on expiry,
        on a successful join, and on reboot. A permanently open network
        lets any device in radio range join.

endmenu
